  "acceptance": "Realize the round-5 metric-measure growth interface on a concrete GEOMETRIC family, closing the 'manifold volume' half of the missing U9 input at the level of one fully verified model. Context: release/Poincare/L4/Compactness/MeasureGrowthChain.lean (leader, round 5) defines the data structure UniformMeasureGrowth (a constructed measure on each member of a family t : Set GHSpace plus scale-uniform doubling C, non-collapsing m, comparability K and an exhaustion radius R) and proves UniformMeasureGrowth => totallyBounded/isCompact/pointed-GH-subsequence with explicit certificates. Its only inhabitant is the degenerate one-point family. Required content: (1) construct, for a concrete compact geometric family, an actual measure and prove it is a genuine inhabitant of that structure with EXPLICIT constants. Recommended target (choose one and justify in the header): the family of round circles of radius r in [1,2] in the plane, with arc-length/Haar measure on AddCircle r (mathlib has Haar measure and the metric on AddCircle), proving the halving-form measure doubling for every centre and every real scale, the non-collapsing lower bound m(s) = min(s, pi) (or a correct explicit analogue), comparability, and the uniform exhaustion radius; alternatively the flat 2-torus family or the family of unit spheres of fixed dimension with normalized area measure. The family must have at least one non-degenerate member (prove a theorem exhibiting two points at positive distance and a ball whose measure genuinely depends on the radius). (2) Downstream checked use: apply the leader's totallyBounded_of_uniformMeasureGrowth / isCompact_of_uniformMeasureGrowth / exists_pointed_subseq_of_uniformMeasureGrowth to this family, so the geometric family is proved compact in GHSpace (closedness included) and has a pointed GH convergent subsequence with an explicit certificate; those leader theorems must be consumed, not reproved. (3) If the construction is genuinely blocked by a missing mathlib API, the deliverable is still mandatory: a compiling blocker module naming the exact missing API (name-level #check probes) plus whatever partial construction does compile (e.g. the measure alone, or the ball-volume formula alone), and a precise list of the remaining obligations. Forbidden: assuming ball growth, doubling, or Bishop-Gromov as a hypothesis of the headline; assuming the conclusion (compactness/pointed convergence) as a hypothesis; statement-only Props as inputs; sorry/axiom/unsafe/native_decide/proof_wanted. Acceptance evidence: compiling modules with full signatures, source hashes, compile exits, fail-closed axiom audit with cones subset {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}, a non-degeneracy theorem, the consumed leader theorems visible in the proof terms, an expanded-hypotheses list classifying every input, and an adversarial semantic review confirming no manifold-level claim beyond the concrete family proved and no circularity. Semantic class: proved/model (concrete geometric family), with chart/model versus manifold claims kept explicit; no general Riemannian-manifold measure is claimed.",
  "expected_evidence": "compiling realization module(s) + explicit-constant proofs + non-degeneracy theorem + downstream application of the leader chain + hashes/exits/axiom audit + must-not-assume list + semantic review; fallback blocker module naming missing mathlib API",
